## Project memory (team-brain)

This repo has a knowledge base: a graph of the entities this project touches
(`inputs/memory/knowledge_graph.yaml`), each linked to a markdown context file holding
the details, gotchas and verbatim code that the code itself does not state.

**Before answering any question about a named entity in this repo - or about what
feeds what, what breaks if something changes, or what we already know about
something - invoke `/team-brain:team-brain` first.** Do not answer from the code
alone, and do not conclude that something does not exist without checking the graph.

Also invoke it when the user says "remember this", "record the learning", "save to
the knowledge base", or corrects a fact about an entity.

All memory lives in this knowledge base. Do not use Claude Code's built-in auto
memory in this repo.

**Saved prompts live in `prompts.md` at the repo root.** When the user says "run the
<name> prompt", "rerun my daily ...", "do the usual ...", or "save this as a prompt",
invoke `/team-brain:team-brain` - it finds the matching prompt by name and runs it.

